{#- Traceability coverage — a self-contained report rendered from the needs index.

    Render it with `ubc report traceability_coverage.html.j2`
    (writes reports/_build/traceability_coverage.html), or from VS Code's
    Reports view via "Generate & Preview" / "Open in Browser".

    HOW IT READS THE CHAIN — worth knowing before you change it.
    A report template cannot walk links: `ubc report` builds each need in the
    Jinja context from that need's scalar FIELDS, so `id`, `type`, `title`,
    `status`, `tags`, `doctype` and the project's `[[needs.extra_options]]` are
    reachable while every LINK field (`satisfies`, `refines`, `verifies`,
    `results_for`, …) is absent. Reading `n.verifies` yields undefined, and the
    usual `(n.verifies or [])` guard turns that into an empty list — so a
    link-based coverage report renders clean and reports 0 % everywhere.
    This template therefore reads the `chain_reqs` extra field that
    `tools/import_test_results.py` stamps on every generated `test_result`: the
    requirement ids that result is evidence for, already resolved through
    `test -> swreq -> arch -> req`. Fields are visible to a template; links are not.

    Script-free by design — pure inline SVG with native <title> tooltips — so it
    renders identically in the editor preview, a browser, and print.

    Colour: the three requirement states and the two test outcomes are STATUS,
    not categories, so they use a fixed status palette and are never themed. Every
    status colour is paired with a glyph and a text label, so colour never carries
    meaning alone. Chart chrome follows the editor theme via --vscode-* variables.
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Traceability Coverage</title>
<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;
    --font: var(--vscode-font-family, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif);
    --surface: var(--vscode-editor-background, #fcfcfb);
    --ink: var(--vscode-foreground, #0b0b0b);
    --ink-2: #52514e;
    --ink-muted: #898781;
    --border: var(--vscode-panel-border, rgba(11, 11, 11, 0.10));
    --soft: var(--vscode-editor-inactiveSelectionBackground, #f0efec);
    /* Status palette — fixed, never themed. */
    --st-good: #0ca30c;
    --st-warning: #fab219;
    --st-serious: #ec835a;
    --st-critical: #d03b3b;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --surface: var(--vscode-editor-background, #1a1a19);
      --ink: var(--vscode-foreground, #ffffff);
      --ink-2: #c3c2b7;
      --border: var(--vscode-panel-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10));
      --soft: var(--vscode-editor-inactiveSelectionBackground, #262c36);
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --surface: var(--vscode-editor-background, #1a1a19);
    --ink: var(--vscode-foreground, #ffffff);
    --ink-2: #c3c2b7;
    --border: var(--vscode-panel-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10));
    --soft: var(--vscode-editor-inactiveSelectionBackground, #262c36);
  }

  body {
    font-family: var(--font); background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 940px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem; line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 .25rem; }
  .sub { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .85rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  code { background: var(--soft); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: .85em; }

  .tiles { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  .tile { flex: 1 1 210px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: .85rem 1rem; }
  .tile .k { font-size: .72rem; color: var(--ink-2); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; margin: 0; }
  .tile .v { font-size: 1.9rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.15; margin: .15rem 0 0; }
  .tile .n { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--ink-muted); margin: .1rem 0 0; }

  figure { margin: 0; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .bar-value { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 620; fill: #ffffff; }

  .legend { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: .6rem 0 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem 1.4rem; }
  .legend li { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .4rem; font-size: .83rem; }
  .legend li.zero { opacity: .55; }
  .swatch { width: .7rem; height: .7rem; border-radius: 2px; flex: none; transform: translateY(1px); }
  .glyph { font-weight: 700; width: 1em; text-align: center; flex: none; }
  .cnt { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 620; }
  .why { color: var(--ink-muted); }

  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: .82rem; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: .4rem .5rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--soft); font-weight: 620; white-space: nowrap; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .state { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 620; }
  dl.defs { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: .25rem 1rem 1rem; }
  dl.defs dt { font-weight: 620; margin-top: .85rem; font-size: .85rem; }
  dl.defs dd { margin: .15rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .85rem; }
  .chain { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

{#- ── Inputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{% set reqs = needs_list | selectattr('type', 'equalto', 'req') | list %}
{% set results = needs_list | selectattr('type', 'equalto', 'test_result') | list %}
{% set req_total = reqs | length %}

{#- The three states a requirement can be in, worst first: the reader should meet
    the problems before the passes. `no_evidence` deliberately merges "no chain at
    all" with "a chain whose tests have no recorded outcome" — both present as zero
    results, and `chain_reqs` cannot tell them apart, so claiming otherwise would
    be a guess. -#}
{% set bucket_defs = [
  {'key': 'failing',     'label': 'Failing evidence',  'status': 'critical', 'glyph': '✕',
   'meaning': 'a recorded outcome reaching this requirement is not `passed`'},
  {'key': 'no_evidence', 'label': 'No test evidence',  'status': 'serious',  'glyph': '⊘',
   'meaning': 'no recorded test outcome reaches this requirement at all'},
  {'key': 'verified',    'label': 'Verified',          'status': 'good',     'glyph': '✓',
   'meaning': 'outcomes reach this requirement and every one of them passed'}
] %}

{#- ── Per-requirement roll-up ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{% set agg = namespace(rows=[], verified=0, failing=0, no_evidence=0) %}
{% for r in reqs %}
  {% set row = namespace(passed=0, failed=0, failing_ids=[]) %}
  {% for t in results %}
    {% if r.id in (t.chain_reqs | default('') | split(', ') | list) %}
      {% if t.outcome == 'passed' %}
        {% set row.passed = row.passed + 1 %}
      {% else %}
        {% set row.failed = row.failed + 1 %}
        {% set row.failing_ids = row.failing_ids + [t.id] %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% if row.failed > 0 %}
    {% set bucket = 'failing' %}{% set agg.failing = agg.failing + 1 %}
  {% elif row.passed > 0 %}
    {% set bucket = 'verified' %}{% set agg.verified = agg.verified + 1 %}
  {% else %}
    {% set bucket = 'no_evidence' %}{% set agg.no_evidence = agg.no_evidence + 1 %}
  {% endif %}
  {% set agg.rows = agg.rows + [{'id': r.id, 'title': r.title, 'status': r.status,
                                 'bucket': bucket, 'passed': row.passed,
                                 'failed': row.failed, 'failing_ids': row.failing_ids}] %}
{% endfor %}

{% set counts = {'failing': agg.failing, 'no_evidence': agg.no_evidence, 'verified': agg.verified} %}
{% set with_chain = agg.verified + agg.failing %}

{#- ── Test-level tally, for comparison ────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{% set tests_passed = results | selectattr('outcome', 'equalto', 'passed') | list | length %}
{% set tests_other = (results | length) - tests_passed %}
{% set test_defs = [
  {'key': 'passed',     'label': 'Passed',     'status': 'good',     'glyph': '✓',
   'count': tests_passed, 'meaning': 'recorded outcome is `passed`'},
  {'key': 'not_passed', 'label': 'Not passed', 'status': 'critical', 'glyph': '✕',
   'count': tests_other, 'meaning': 'recorded outcome is failed, error or skipped'}
] %}

{#- ── Stacked-bar geometry. Zero-count segments are dropped rather than drawn as
       a hairline of colour that reads as a real value. ───────────────────────── -#}
{% set BAR = 720 %}{% set GAP = 2 %}{% set LABEL_MIN = 44 %}

{% macro stacked_bar(items, total, clip_id, aria) %}
  {% set vis = namespace(list=[]) %}
  {% for b in items %}{% if b.count > 0 %}{% set vis.list = vis.list + [b] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ BAR }} 30" role="img" aria-label="{{ aria }}">
    <defs><clipPath id="{{ clip_id }}"><rect x="0" y="0" width="{{ BAR }}" height="28" rx="4"/></clipPath></defs>
    {% set cur = namespace(x=0) %}
    <g clip-path="url(#{{ clip_id }})">
      {% for b in vis.list %}
        {% set raw = b.count / total * BAR %}
        {% set w = BAR - cur.x if loop.last else (raw - GAP if raw > GAP + 1 else 1) %}
        <rect x="{{ cur.x | round(2) }}" y="0" width="{{ w | round(2) }}" height="28"
              fill="var(--st-{{ b.status }})">
          <title>{{ b.label }}: {{ b.count }} of {{ total }} ({{ (b.count / total * 100) | round(1) }} %)</title>
        </rect>
        {% if w >= LABEL_MIN %}
        <text class="bar-value" x="{{ (cur.x + w / 2) | round(2) }}" y="19" text-anchor="middle">{{ b.count }}</text>
        {% endif %}
        {% set cur.x = cur.x + raw %}
      {% endfor %}
    </g>
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro legend(items, total) %}
  <ul class="legend">
    {% for b in items %}
    <li{% if b.count == 0 %} class="zero"{% endif %}>
      <span class="swatch" style="background: var(--st-{{ b.status }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="glyph" style="color: var(--st-{{ b.status }})" aria-hidden="true">{{ b.glyph }}</span>
      <span><span class="cnt">{{ b.count }}</span> {{ b.label }}</span>
      <span class="why">&mdash; {{ b.meaning }}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endmacro %}

{#- ── Page ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
<h1>Traceability Coverage</h1>
<p class="sub">
  {{ req_total }} system requirements &middot; {{ needs | length }} needs in the graph
  {% if results | length > 0 %}
  &middot; test evidence from run <code>{{ (results | first).test_run_label }}</code>
  {% endif %}
</p>

{% if req_total == 0 %}
<p><em>No system requirements found. Index the project and re-run this report.</em></p>
{% else %}

<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile">
    <p class="k">Full chain to a test</p>
    <p class="v">{{ with_chain }} / {{ req_total }}</p>
    <p class="n">
      {{ (with_chain / req_total * 100) | round(1) }} % of system requirements are reached
      by at least one recorded test outcome
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile">
    <p class="k">Passing : non-passing</p>
    <p class="v">
      {% if agg.failing > 0 %}{{ (agg.verified / agg.failing) | round(1) }} : 1{% else %}{{ agg.verified }} : 0{% endif %}
    </p>
    <p class="n">
      of the {{ with_chain }} with evidence, {{ agg.verified }} all-passing
      vs {{ agg.failing }} with a failure
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile">
    <p class="k">No evidence at all</p>
    <p class="v">{{ agg.no_evidence }} / {{ req_total }}</p>
    <p class="n">{{ (agg.no_evidence / req_total * 100) | round(1) }} % have no recorded outcome reaching them</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>System requirements by evidence state</h2>
<p class="sub">Each requirement falls in exactly one state. Hover a segment for its share.</p>
<figure>
  {% set req_items = [] %}
  {% set ri = namespace(list=[]) %}
  {% for b in bucket_defs %}
    {% set ri.list = ri.list + [{'key': b.key, 'label': b.label, 'status': b.status,
                                 'glyph': b.glyph, 'meaning': b.meaning, 'count': counts[b.key]}] %}
  {% endfor %}
  {{ stacked_bar(ri.list, req_total, 'clip-req', 'System requirements by evidence state') }}
  {{ legend(ri.list, req_total) }}
</figure>

<h2>Recorded test outcomes</h2>
<p class="sub">
  The test-case level, for comparison: {{ results | length }} recorded results,
  {% if results | length > 0 %}{{ (tests_passed / (results | length) * 100) | round(1) }} %{% else %}0 %{% endif %}
  passing.
</p>
<figure>
  {% if results | length > 0 %}
  {{ stacked_bar(test_defs, results | length, 'clip-test', 'Recorded test outcomes') }}
  {{ legend(test_defs, results | length) }}
  {% else %}
  <p><em>No test results imported. Run <code>tools/import_test_results.py</code>.</em></p>
  {% endif %}
</figure>

<h2>What this measures</h2>
<dl class="defs">
  <dt>Full chain to a test</dt>
  <dd>
    A recorded test outcome reaches the requirement through
    <span class="chain">req &larr;satisfies&mdash; arch &larr;refines&mdash; swreq &larr;verifies&mdash; test &larr;results_for&mdash; test_result</span>.
    That chain is resolved by <code>tools/import_test_results.py</code> and stamped on
    each <code>test_result</code> as its <code>chain_reqs</code> field, because a report
    template can read fields but cannot follow links.
  </dd>
  <dt>Why “no test evidence” merges two cases</dt>
  <dd>
    A requirement with no architecture beneath it and a requirement whose tests
    have never been run both present as zero recorded outcomes.
    <code>chain_reqs</code> cannot separate them, so they share one state rather
    than being guessed apart. Use <code>ubc agent gaps</code> to tell which is which:
    a structural hole shows there, an unrun test does not.
  </dd>
  {% for b in bucket_defs %}
  <dt><span class="glyph" style="color: var(--st-{{ b.status }})" aria-hidden="true">{{ b.glyph }}</span> {{ b.label }}</dt>
  <dd>{{ b.meaning }}</dd>
  {% endfor %}
</dl>

<h2>Every system requirement</h2>
<p class="sub">Worst state first. This table is also the accessible view of both charts above.</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>State</th>
      <th>Requirement</th>
      <th class="num">passed</th>
      <th class="num">failed</th>
      <th>Failing evidence</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for b in bucket_defs %}
      {% for row in agg.rows %}
        {% if row.bucket == b.key %}
        <tr>
          <td class="state" style="color: var(--st-{{ b.status }})">
            <span aria-hidden="true">{{ b.glyph }}</span> {{ b.label }}
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>{{ row.id }}</code><br>
            <span class="muted">{{ row.title }}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="num">{{ row.passed }}</td>
          <td class="num">{% if row.failed > 0 %}{{ row.failed }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="chain">
            {% for fid in row.failing_ids %}{{ fid }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem">
  Rendered from <code>needs.json</code>. Rebuild the graph with <code>ubc build needs</code>;
  refresh the test evidence with
  <code>python3 -m pytest -q --junitxml=reports/junit/testresults.xml</code> followed by
  <code>python3 tools/import_test_results.py</code>.
</p>

{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
